    "id": "c08",
    "store": "saffron-loom",
    "storeName": "Saffron Loom Textiles",
    "request": "What's a sensible return window for handloom sarees?",
    "made": {
      "kind": "reply",
      "text": "**A 7-day return window from delivery works well for handloom sarees**, with exchanges allowed up to about 15 days. That gives buyers time to see the drape and colour in person. It also keeps the saree from going out of season, or being worn for an occasion and then sent back.\n\nA few conditions make that window work:\n\n- **Unused and as sent:** unworn, unwashed, tags on, original packaging.\n- **Blouse piece uncut:** once it's cut or stitched, the saree can't be returned.\n- **No fall, pico or tailoring done:** this is often the clearest sign it's been used.\n- **Final sale on custom or altered pieces:** this includes made-to-order weaves and sarees with stitched blouses.\n- **Small variations aren't defects:** slight colour differences, uneven weave and small slubs are part of handloom. Say so on product pages so these don't come back as \"faulty\" returns.\n- **Real defects have no deadline worry:** a tear, stain or wrong item should get a free return or replacement as long as it's reported within 48 hours of delivery.\n\nIf you want, I can turn this into a written return policy for your store.",
